      <section class="editorial-chapter">
        <h2>Selection Grade &amp; Special Grade Rules: The 10 &amp; 20 Year Increments</h2>
        <p>
          A defining feature of the Tamil Nadu public compensation framework is the statutory provision for <strong>Selection Grade and Special Grade promotions</strong>. Governed under paragraph 6 of G.O. Ms. No. 303, this scheme protects state employees from career stagnation:
        </p>
        <div class="callout-box">
          <h4>The 10 and 20 Year Career Advancement Rule:</h4>
          <ul class="bullet-feature-list">
            <li><strong>Selection Grade (On Completing 10 Years):</strong> An employee serving in Levels 1 through 23 who completes 10 years of continuous service in a single post without regular promotion is awarded Selection Grade. The employee is granted <strong>two vertical increments (a 6% cumulative base increase)</strong> within the same level.</li>
            <li><strong>Special Grade (On Completing 20 Years):</strong> An employee who remains in the same post for 20 years without regular promotion is awarded Special Grade, which grants an additional <strong>two vertical increments</strong>.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            This mechanism ensures that employees in operational and clerical cadres receive substantial pay progression even when departmental promotion vacancies are unavailable.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="editorial-chapter">
        <h2>City Classification and HRA Slabs in Tamil Nadu</h2>
        <p>
          In Tamil Nadu, House Rent Allowance (HRA) is administered under state-specific city grading orders issued by the Finance Department:
        </p>
        <div class="city-classification-grid">
          <div class="city-box tier-chennai">
            <h4>Grade I(a) - Greater Chennai</h4>
            <div class="badge-tag">Greater Chennai Corporation Limits</div>
            <p><strong>Projected HRA Rate:</strong> 27% of Basic Pay (or enhanced ceiling rate).</p>
            <p><strong>Covered Areas:</strong> Chennai City, contiguous municipal zones, and Greater Chennai Police limits.</p>
            <span class="card-footer-note">Reflects the highest residential rental cost bracket in Tamil Nadu.</span>
          </div>

          <div class="city-box tier-grade1b">
            <h4>Grade I(b) - Major Corporations</h4>
            <div class="badge-tag">Population 5 Lakh to 50 Lakh</div>
            <p><strong>Projected HRA Rate:</strong> 18% of Basic Pay.</p>
            <p><strong>Covered Cities:</strong> Coimbatore, Madurai, Tiruchirappalli, Salem, Tirunelveli, and Tiruppur.</p>
            <span class="card-footer-note">Covers major industrial and educational municipal corporations.</span>
          </div>

